  "details": "In particular, the string constructor node causes the problem when set to sbyte* and char*. Old graphs are capable of working with the node, but the compile fails. As a result they are capable of repairing the problem if you know what it is. But new graphs are entirely unable to render the node (or anything afterwards, such as flow lines) so there is no way to fix it without going back to old graphs.",
